kese wa shinai sa

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:54.180
...will ever take it away

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:05.300
episode

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:05.300
Will the Dead Man's Chest
\h    Shine on a Full-Moon?!

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:15.700
Come on, let's go!

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:18.660
Go, Benbow!

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.890
Silver.
I brought you coconuts.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.390
Great, thanks.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.700
That's cold!

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.440
Delicious!

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.080
You feeling better?

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.100
Thanks to you, I'm feeling much better.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.000
I'm grateful to all of you.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.700
It's because of me that you've chosen a cave close to the sea.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.200
It's really been long since I was able to rest.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.540
Hey, come have a look!
We've brought back algae!

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.900
That's great!

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.670
So it is. We'll be able to make a good soup tonight.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.930
Are we that pressed for food?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:32.460
Yeah, ever since a day or three.
We've used up the supplies from the ship.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.860
But it's not that serious. We can find things to eat on the island.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.830
That may be so for now,
but it'll soon be the rainy season.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:44.770
During the rainy season,
it rains day and night.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:47.370
We won't even be able to
go out and search for food.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:55.790
It'll be a full-moon in a night or two.
We must find Flint's Mansion before then.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:09.020
<i>Silver has proposed that
we split into two groups.</i>

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.980
<i>The first group consists of Ben Gunn as guide,</i>

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.850
<i>Dr. Livesey,</i>

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.220
<i>Mr. Trelawney...</i>

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.460
<i>...and Captain Smollett.</i>

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.500
<i>The second group obviously consists of Silver and I.</i>

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.860
<i>Additionally, we'll be escorted by Gray.</i>

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:26.820
<i>As for Hunter, he will be in charge of watching Silver.</i>

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:32.340
And me... What team will be graced by my presence?

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.670
Whichever you want.
You get to choose.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:36.000
Let's go, Silver.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.860
Good luck, doctor.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.100
Team one or two?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.130
It's too hard to decide!

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.500
Let's see here.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.440
I should think about this, for sure!

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:48.460
Any way you look at it, I'm their prisoner.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.460
Therefore, it's better if I'm seen
doing good in front of Trelawney.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.300
That's it!

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.020
But wait...

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.540
If I ever mess up, they could change their minds.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.480
What if they take me to the police when we return?

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.580
I should really follow the others.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.120
Safety comes first!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.830
Wait, Jim!

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.880
<i>And so, whether we find the treasure or not,</i>

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.800
<i>we must return to the fort at nightfall.</i>

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.500
<i>"A bell on a full-moon night..."</i>

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.980
<i>"The mansion of Flint..."</i>

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.900
<i>"45 degrees with a spyglass on the Devil's Throne..."</i>

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:30.730
<i>"Aim the light through
the left eye of the skull."</i>

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:34.140
Flint's Mansion, Flint's Mansion...

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:41.700
I was thinking... there might be a swamp in the shape of an F of "Flint".

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.060
I see.
That is possible.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.620
Good thinking, Jim.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.550
I don't think it'd be that simple, though.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:05.010
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest!

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.930
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of r—

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.440
Wait a second...

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:21.250
Even if Silver is still recovering,
it may have been wrong to separate.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.330
Why is that?

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:25.810
Well, here's why...
He's a genius at deceiving people.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:29.610
The smaller the group, the more influence he'll have over them.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.010
You think he'll do it again?

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.130
Absolutely, it's what he does best!

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:37.480
Don't worry. Gray and Hunter are men worthy of our trust.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:41.520
Flint's Mansion... Flint's Mansion...

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.840
Hey, Puppy!
Be a little more serious!

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:49.570
Even if you find it, I won't get anything.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.530
Hey there, Gray and Hunter!

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.650
I was joking just now.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:59.200
Don't say anything to
Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.570
Okay, okay?
Okay?!

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:04.290
Puppy, don't worry.
They're gentlemen.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.070
We'll get our share, you and I.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:15.030
And if they refuse, I'll find a way.
Right, Gray?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.130
Let me tell you one thing, Silver.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:25.210
What you think and say doesn't interest me.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.680
The fact is, you're our prisoner.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:30.890
You are supposed to solve this riddle.

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:34.410
If you try anything else,
I'll shoot without warning.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.260
I thought guns weren't
your weapon of choice?

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:39.810
Surely you'd prefer to drive one of your knives through my heart.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:42.480
Too bad.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.230
Before your knife even reaches its target,
my right pulls off a "nice catch".

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:52.060
Your knives are much slower than those of my old friend Flint.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.620
You looking for a fight?

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.250
Stop it, both of you!
What are you doing?!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.490
You're wasting time!

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:03.890
Gray, we must search for Flint's Mansion!

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.460
Silver, you are supposed to solve this riddle of the full-moon!

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:09.770
There's no time to lose!

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.100
Now, get moving!

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.810
Mr. Trelawney's group are
doing everything they can!

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.760
I'm also doing everything I can, Hunter...

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:18.510
But...

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.680
I'm fed up with being treated this way!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.360
Just thinking about it makes me mad.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.150
Look, we won't find anything by traversing the island to and fro.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.150
I'm thinking about the riddle while walking.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:43.650
It's a battle between Flint's mind and mine.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:47.330
I don't want to be disturbed by two guard dogs!

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.400
Wait.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:16.360
Jim, you think that this "Mansion" could be in the swamp, don't you?

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:18.280
Yes, that's right.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.720
A swamp doesn't sound quite right...

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:24.950
The sea!
The sea seems much more likely.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.220
Flint was a pirate.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:33.250
The sea was his element.
We must search for it there.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.550
Yes...

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:39.330
We've searched every corner of the island,

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:43.080
but we haven't thought to search in the sea.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:57.910
Everyone to the shore!

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.870
We must search along the shore!

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.800
Of course, that's it!

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:24.570
Flint's Mansion may be a pirate ship that lies at the bottom of the sea.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:27.050
It could be possible.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:29.770
In any case, there must be something on the surface,

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.270
or in the sea that's visible offshore.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:50.250
Jim!

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.500
Silver!

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:55.510
A shark!

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.120
Silver!

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:30.380
Silver!

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:13.350
You alright, Jim?

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.890
I just swallowed some seawater.
I'm okay.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:23.520
<i>I see...
So that's it.</i>

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.470
<i>I've solved Flint's riddle.</i>

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:34.960
You've solved the riddle of the "Mansion of Flint"?

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.560
Yes...
I finally understand.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.790
Truthfully, I don't know where it is yet.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.740
But I know what we're looking for.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.290
So what must we look for, Silver?

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:52.250
Flint was known as
"The Shark of the Caribbean".

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:54.290
"Emperor of the Seas",

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:55.380
"Messenger of the Devil",

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:56.740
"Captain White Bone".

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:58.730
He had a number of aliases.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:03.180
But what he became knows as after he sank six Spanish warships...

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.180
...was "The Shark of the Caribbean."

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.720
This name suited him perfectly.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:14.690
"The Shark".
Yes, he was vicious like a shark.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:21.030
"The Mansion of Flint"...

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.670
In other words, "The Mansion of Sharks"{ is what it means}.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.860
"The Mansion of Sharks"?

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.030
Listen, no one sleeps tonight.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.080
We'll need everyone to work hard together.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.560
We're going to build a raft.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:35.790
At dawn, we'll head out to sea to look for "The Mansion of Sharks".

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:38.750
Silver, what is "The Mansion of Sharks"?

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.710
Indeed, I don't see what you mean.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.980
This "Mansion" is a den of sharks.

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:50.390
A den of sharks?

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:54.110
Yes, sharks are such strange creatures.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:58.230
It is said that they spend their lives
swimming in the ocean,

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.550
never resting.

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:03.250
For a motionless shark, is a dead shark.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:18.670
But in reality, even sharks must rest.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.600
And they do so in their "Mansions".

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:25.200
Few have been seen by wolves of the sea.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.590
This means they are rare.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.550
But Flint must have found one.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:33.010
Somewhere offshore of the island.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.720
Got it?
Don't stray from the raft.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:41.560
Return to the raft the moment you see a shark.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.440
If you don't, your life will be forfeit.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:10.260
Shark Shark

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:10.630
Shark Shark

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:11.050
Shark Shark

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:11.430
Shark Shark

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:11.800
Shark Shark

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.220
Shark Shark

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:12.640
Shark Shark

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:13.050
Shark Shark

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.220
Shar—

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:40.520
God, it's beautiful...

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:43.880
Really, it's been a long time since I've had fun like this.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.190
And, have you found a clue to this mansion of sharks?

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.260
Oh, I forgot.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.240
Sorry, it slipped my mind.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.010
Where are Jim and Gray?

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:56.930
They're still having fun.
Yes, that's it.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.780
A shark is here!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:42.560
GRAY!

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:53.990
GRAY!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.070
It's Gray!

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.570
Gray!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.440
I've found the Mansion of Sharks.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:17.660
But, it's not one of their dens.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.600
It's a cemetery of sharks.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.150
A cemetery of sharks?

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:24.420
Seems like old Flint alright!

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:29.220
And the Devil's Throne is just above it.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:41.510
I see, so that's the Devil's Throne...

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.890
"A bell on a full-moon night."
"The mansion of Flint."

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:55.570
"45 degrees with a spyglass on the Devil's Throne."

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.010
"Aim the light through
the left eye of the skull."

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:00.570
So that's what it meant, Old Flint.

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:07.370
Silver, soon it will be half past midnight.

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:10.330
Okay, leave it to me!

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:14.700
"45 degrees with a spyglass on the Devil's Throne."

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.460
That's it...

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:22.220
And now, aiming the light...

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.180
Silver, it's half past midnight!

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.480
<i>Over there!</i>

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:09.770
Captain Smollett, what is the next phrase?

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:13.520
"Aim the light through
the left eye of the skull."

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.980
Thought so.

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:19.900
Over there!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.870
Look, there's a bow and arrow.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:33.650
We probably have to fire through the left eye of the skull.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:36.840
That will put an end to all this.
Jim!

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:41.800
You should complete this final trial.

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:46.610
I'm impressed you've made it this far...

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:50.220
I want to show my respect as fellow man.

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:53.600
Silver...

00:21:58.360 --> 00:22:00.110
This is more than I ever imagined...

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:07.470
Incredible.

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:09.890
It's like he scoured the earth for all its treasures.

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:16.810
This is it, mother!
I've finally found it.

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:19.160
Treasure, treasure!
Treasure!

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:21.260
Treasure, treasure!

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:24.730
Treasure, treasure!
Treasure!

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:27.130
Treasure, treasure!

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:32.120
To      be        continued

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.210
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.210
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:44.020
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:44.020
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:50.230
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:50.230
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.230 --> 00:22:55.670
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.230 --> 00:22:55.670
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.670 --> 00:23:01.080
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.670 --> 00:23:01.080
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:06.540
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:06.540
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:12.170
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:12.170
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:18.030
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:18.030
Will be brought back

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:24.620
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:24.620
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:30.510
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:30.510
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:40.230
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:40.230
